    <innernamespace refid="namespacenexus">nexus</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Interprocess protocol message types. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Defines the message kind enumeration used by Channel and Link to identify messages exchanged over JUCE&apos;s <ref refid="classInterprocessConnection" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">InterprocessConnection</ref> (TCP).</para>
<para>Wire format inside each JUCE IPC frame: uint16_t kind (LE) | payload bytes.</para>
<sect1 id="_message_8h_1autotoc_md16_1s1"><sect2 id="_message_8h_1autotoc_md16_1s2"><sect3 id="_message_8h_1autotoc_md16">
<title>Wire protocol</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>createSession(shell, args, cwd, uuid, cols, rows, envID)</computeroutput> — client→daemon; daemon creates if uuid is new, resizes+attaches if uuid exists</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>loading(uuid, bytes)</computeroutput> — daemon→client initial byte snapshot for the loading phase</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>output(uuid, bytes)</computeroutput> — daemon→client live PTY bytes</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>input(uuid, bytes)</computeroutput> — client→daemon keyboard/mouse input</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>resizeSession(uuid, cols, rows)</computeroutput> — client→daemon</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>detachSession(uuid)</computeroutput> — client→daemon &quot;stop forwarding&quot; (session keeps running)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>killSession(uuid)</computeroutput> — client→daemon &quot;kill this shell&quot; (session destroyed)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>sessionKilled(uuid)</computeroutput> — daemon→client &quot;shell exited&quot;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>sessions(uuids)</computeroutput> — daemon→client initial session list on hello</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>stateUpdate(uuid, cwd, fgProcess)</computeroutput> — daemon→client state sync (cwd + foreground process)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>hello</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>helloResponse</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>ping</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>pong</computeroutput> — control </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect3></sect2></sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
